  "_commit": {
    "id": "0527f8b69726190c6447809e1c56219ad08dd193",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Move spatialdataR support into R/, fix the SFE and SpatialData seams\n\nThe spatialdataR integration now lives in R/ with its tests (it was an\ninst/scripts file), registers into private environments, and follows\nboth optional packages through load, reload and unload. An independent\nfive-lens review of the SFE and spatialdataR seams drove most of the\nfixes below.\n\nRegistration\n- Hooks are tagged, replaced on reload instead of stacking, and removed\n  by a new .onUnload.\n- A failed registration warns, naming the package and the cause, instead\n  of printing a bare hook error.\n- The \"registered\" record is tied to the loaded namespace of the\n  optional package, so unloading and reloading SpatialFeatureExperiment\n  or spatialdataR re-registers instead of silently losing the methods.\n\nSpatialData\n- Fix a shapes element coming back with no rows: tables now carry their\n  region and instance keys in int_colData, where spatialdataR keeps and\n  reads them, elements declare their instance_key, and a table read from\n  spatialdataR is read the same way. A layer that still loses rows\n  warns.\n- Link points and shapes to a table through the table's instance_key,\n  whatever the column is called.\n- Carry the CRS of points and shapes over; it was dropped silently.\n- Remove the DuckDB tables a failed conversion wrote.\n- Make the accessors agree with spatialdataR: a bad name or position is\n  an error, NULL empties a layer, element<- takes a position, and\n  point(x, 10) <- v no longer invents an element. Add replacement\n  methods for the image, label, point and shape names; the spatialMap\n  follows a rename.\n- Warn that sample-level colData is dropped going to SpatialData.\n\nSpatialFeatureExperiment\n- spatialGraphs, spatialGraph and spatialGraphNames honour sample_id and\n  return the shapes SFE does.\n- findDebrisCells returns a MultiAssaySpatialExperiment, and\n  localResults agrees with localResultNames.\n- Keep the metadata of the SFE and each sample's graph weight style\n  through the round t",
    "time": 1794854663
  },
